# T3 on the RTX 3090 at the serving defaults (the Qwen3.8 serve seat, place a, the MTP draft under its cost-chosen width,
# adaptive residency mid-p0-s1 and the expert stream), prose 3840. The seat pins its caller (BLOOMERY_PIN_MAIN), so the pool has a
# CCD map. Derived [design-t3, probe S-T3a]: a window layer is front 312.8 + max(shadow 130.5, host 12 + 11.43 x W) + back 86.7
# us (the evaluator's server preset, 37.45 ms a window at W 23.36); the warm walks front + back - 10 us at 125..134 GB/s less the
# residency lane's copies in the same gap (0..12.3 MB, from the tournament's 10..19 landings a token, unmeasured): 11.6..16.7
# experts; the predictor's recall over the first 96 rows of a prose request at B 10..15 is 0.28..0.35 (design-t3 recall5: the
# table reset at the prompt call, fed the kept rows, cap 16, plus last); the cut a layer is 11.43 x r x (W - c_hot), under the
# host's 148.5 us excess over the shadow.
# c_hot is MEASURED: 11.28 us a warmed expert against 24.68 cold (specs/leader/t3probe/result.md), where the design's band
# assumed 5..12 and its centre 9. The design's sensitivity table (server, centre recall): +8.5 % at c_hot 9, +6.6 % at 12, so
# +7.1 % at 11.28 by linear interpolation [derived]; c_hot 10.6..12.0 (the fit's k = 3 miss) gives +6.6..+7.7 %. The card's band
# is the draft's recall spread (5..12 about an 8.5 centre, x0.59..x1.41) on the new centre: 7.1 x 0.59..1.41 = 4.2..10.0
# [derived]. Changed = ours (warm on), base = ours@BLOOMERY_HOST_WARM=off (CCD lanes on); @BLOOMERY_HOST_LANES=flat separates
# R1's own price (the probe: +1.2 % ms/token at k = 0 on the leg) from R2's gain.
# Runner gap (stated, not patched; the runner's owner is the lead): tools/ref/q38-3090-server.sh is the 3090 server-shape
# runner (plan a, the draft and residency at their unset defaults, no --place passed), and it refuses any lever set in its
# environment, so the @BLOOMERY_HOST_WARM=off and @BLOOMERY_HOST_LANES=flat arms cannot be carried; it has no arms, rounds,
# paired ratio, bin: arm or lease/card; it reads no timings.predicted_per_second (it reads the chats' records); and the seat
# prints no `stat step`, so warm_recall and warm_mb are unreadable there (the load line's `warm=` word is what shows). A run of
# this card needs the runner to carry an @LEVER=value list per arm, read the predicted_per_second of a 96-token request after a
# 3840-token prompt, and take the card.
kind: ab
question: does the step port's L3 warm cut the Qwen3.8 serve seat's decode window at the serving defaults on the 3090 by the
  derived share?
term: decode tok/s @ n=96 greedy tokens, prompt the first 3840 ids of the prose corpus (the server's
  timings.predicted_per_second), bloomery-serve-qwen38 at its unset defaults (place a on the one 3090, the draft and residency
  on), RTX 3090 at 250 W: ours against ours@BLOOMERY_HOST_WARM=off, paired by round
unit: %
predict: 4.2..10.0
rounds: 4
condition: one lease, a fresh server process an arm and round, the 3090 as BLOOMERY_TIMING_GPU, arms ours,
  ours@BLOOMERY_HOST_WARM=off, ours@BLOOMERY_HOST_LANES=flat and bin:<base tree's bloomery-serve-qwen38>; inside the window:
  every plan record card= the 3090 with the draft and residency on, the load lines `warm=on` on ours, `warm=off why=lever` on the
  off arm and `warm=off why=lanes-flat` on the flat arm; the answers' tokens equal across all arms; majflt equal between the on and off arms; no
  counted row [cold], [cpu-busy] or [other-busy]; the design's recall (0.22..0.42), warm_mb a step (48 x 30..55 MB) and gap_p50
  (330..450 us) are read from the seat's step records only once it prints them
decide-in: land with S-T3b's result; write the 3090 server cell beside the README row
decide-below: below 4.2 %: read the flat arm and the load lines first; straggle or gap up with recall in band means the warm
  crowds the residency lane's window copies (a profile arm with the residency pass records, then cap the warm while the lane
  holds a job); recall under 0.22 re-derives the predictor against the engine's kept rows
decide-above: the cut passes 10.0 %: the overlap form or a larger window; re-derive the band before the README number
